1
00:02:04,399 --> 00:02:08,729
No living creature were hurt during
the production of this show.

2
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:11,770
Brought to you by historicalfuntv.com

3
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:14,180
Who did this?

4
00:02:16,132 --> 00:02:17,259
Who?

5
00:02:17,259 --> 00:02:20,789
We saw Rogatus' flag at the scene, my Bey.

6
00:02:23,857 --> 00:02:27,177
- Bring Karayel, Göktuğ.
- Eyvallah(okay), my Bey.

7
00:02:34,805 --> 00:02:36,055
Ambush!

8
00:02:37,415 --> 00:02:40,575
Brothers, they are attacking
Turgut Bey's alps!

9
00:02:58,223 --> 00:03:00,013
We'll deliver his relics to...

10
00:03:01,754 --> 00:03:03,834
Turgut Bey.

11
00:03:08,599 --> 00:03:10,729
Bury the dead.

12
00:03:11,984 --> 00:03:14,394
Dig graves for traitors!

13
00:03:15,629 --> 00:03:17,519
As you order, my Bey.

14
00:03:52,951 --> 00:03:54,101
My Bey.

15
00:04:02,415 --> 00:04:03,885
Karayel.

16
00:04:24,899 --> 00:04:27,119
Go, brothers, go!

17
00:05:11,491 --> 00:05:12,811
Karayel!

18
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:35,040
Karayel!

19
00:05:44,792 --> 00:05:46,222
Brother!

20
00:05:51,862 --> 00:05:53,262
Brother!

21
00:05:56,605 --> 00:06:00,175
They raided my home,
slaughtered Karayel!

22
00:06:04,775 --> 00:06:06,785
He was from my blood!

23
00:06:07,308 --> 00:06:09,868
They cut my wings, brother!

24
00:06:23,521 --> 00:06:25,461
Now they are telling us...

25
00:06:26,159 --> 00:06:28,349
"We'll not let you stay here...

26
00:06:28,415 --> 00:06:30,595
... we are after you".

27
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,490
What stops the one who...

28
00:06:36,367 --> 00:06:39,287
...raided our base from raiding
my tent?

29
00:06:41,495 --> 00:06:43,525
The one who slaughtered Karayel...

30
00:06:43,747 --> 00:06:46,267
...can slaughter my Orhan tomorrow!

31
00:06:52,684 --> 00:06:54,564
The top is responsible for...

32
00:06:55,001 --> 00:06:57,081
...an alp's mistake.

33
00:06:59,542 --> 00:07:02,332
Water sleeps but the enemy never sleeps.

34
00:07:03,936 --> 00:07:07,016
You are the leader!
Why were you not awake?

35
00:07:09,548 --> 00:07:11,278
Boran!

36
00:07:19,256 --> 00:07:20,479
My Bey.

37
00:07:20,479 --> 00:07:22,769
- Are the horses ready?
- They're ready, my Bey.

38
00:07:22,972 --> 00:07:25,152
We are going to set off right away.

39
00:07:26,123 --> 00:07:28,763
We'll be at Turgut Bey's tent
before sunrise.

40
00:07:30,161 --> 00:07:32,671
We can't make our martyrs wait.

41
00:07:33,296 --> 00:07:34,866
As you command, my Bey.

42
00:07:43,677 --> 00:07:46,187
You are not coming, brother.

43
00:07:50,523 --> 00:07:52,113
What happened happened.

44
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:56,608
We have to be sure who did it.

45
00:07:58,415 --> 00:08:01,105
You'll go to Rogatus, to Bilecik.

46
00:08:02,593 --> 00:08:04,763
Invite him to my tent.

47
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:07,250
We'll look right at his eyes.

48
00:08:07,405 --> 00:08:10,895
We look so that we can see if he did it.

49
00:08:24,431 --> 00:08:26,501
As you command, my Bey.

50
00:08:27,819 --> 00:08:30,899
Turgut Bey Tent.

51
00:08:45,147 --> 00:08:48,137
- Can I come in, my Bey.
- Come, Kutan.

52
00:08:57,633 --> 00:08:59,973
Is there anything about Osman Bey.

53
00:09:00,831 --> 00:09:03,531
No, my Bey.
No one showed up.

54
00:09:06,662 --> 00:09:08,372
They'll come.

55
00:09:08,999 --> 00:09:10,469
They will come.

56
00:09:12,125 --> 00:09:13,695
I hope nothing happ...

57
00:09:13,695 --> 00:09:15,911
They'll come safe and sound Inshallah,
Kutay.

58
00:09:20,542 --> 00:09:23,072
Osman Bey will bring our brothers.

59
00:09:25,557 --> 00:09:27,027
He will.

60
00:09:29,621 --> 00:09:31,381
If he can't...

61
00:09:50,229 --> 00:09:53,199
A proof, just a proof.

62
00:09:54,299 --> 00:09:57,109
A proof of the cruel
who slaughtered Karayel.

63
00:10:51,511 --> 00:10:53,051
Sergeant Ayhan.

64
00:10:53,314 --> 00:10:55,434
My valiant alps!

65
00:10:59,377 --> 00:11:03,577
My Bey, you promised me that my
dad would return!

66
00:11:04,041 --> 00:11:08,221
They not only martyred him,
also cut his fingers!

67
00:11:09,277 --> 00:11:11,057
You promised me!

68
00:11:29,205 --> 00:11:31,245
Damn them all!

69
00:11:31,943 --> 00:11:35,013
They murdered my son!
May Allah curse them!

70
00:11:35,398 --> 00:11:36,908
Osman Bey.

71
00:11:38,912 --> 00:11:42,662
Osman Bey,
in whom all the community trusts.

72
00:11:48,199 --> 00:11:50,289
You couldn't keep your promise.

73
00:11:50,801 --> 00:11:53,021
The Lord tricked you!

74
00:11:53,216 --> 00:11:56,516
Turgut Bey, watch your words!

75
00:11:58,749 --> 00:12:01,489
You are talking to
Ertugrul Ghazi's son Osman Bey.

76
00:12:01,986 --> 00:12:04,196
I kept my promise!

77
00:12:06,353 --> 00:12:09,913
We did right at Kosses issue.

78
00:12:11,734 --> 00:12:13,234
What about my Alps?

79
00:12:14,076 --> 00:12:15,716
What about my fellows?

80
00:12:16,913 --> 00:12:20,633
How did it happen? Tell me Osman Bey.
Who? How?

81
00:12:22,467 --> 00:12:24,047
Vengeance...

82
00:12:25,794 --> 00:12:28,094
...destroys its keeper.

83
00:12:31,513 --> 00:12:33,583
You are the Bey of your tent.

84
00:12:34,787 --> 00:12:36,587
If you burn yourself down...

85
00:12:38,084 --> 00:12:39,984
You'll burn everyone down.

86
00:12:41,473 --> 00:12:44,343
We have nothing to lose, don't you see?

87
00:12:45,089 --> 00:12:47,089
It's time to go all in.

88
00:12:48,689 --> 00:12:51,259
Do not get close to them.

89
00:12:52,488 --> 00:12:55,518
Protect yourself, Osman Bey.

90
00:12:57,132 --> 00:12:58,682
You are being naive.

91
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:04,300
Don't.

92
00:13:12,304 --> 00:13:14,594
We have to take revenge for
our brothers.

93
00:13:17,209 --> 00:13:19,319
Command us to fight, my Bey!

94
00:13:21,797 --> 00:13:24,257
We'll take revenge.

95
00:13:24,991 --> 00:13:27,981
We'll kill that infidel Kosses.

96
00:13:29,498 --> 00:13:31,658
It's not certain if it's Kosses or not.

97
00:13:34,322 --> 00:13:36,182
There's something else.

98
00:13:37,144 --> 00:13:39,304
Let things settle down...

99
00:13:40,807 --> 00:13:43,007
Wait for things to settle down.

100
00:13:43,455 --> 00:13:45,245
So tell me who that was!

101
00:13:45,588 --> 00:13:47,478
Who was it, Osman Bey?

102
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:50,900
I said what I had to said.

103
00:13:53,126 --> 00:13:54,746
Your Alps are now martyrs.

104
00:13:56,770 --> 00:13:59,870
They reached the glorious position
we all want to have.

105
00:14:02,993 --> 00:14:04,693
Now live with your pain.

106
00:14:06,638 --> 00:14:08,978
Bury our martyrs.

107
00:14:12,228 --> 00:14:14,708
So, this is all you have to say...

108
00:14:30,875 --> 00:14:32,595
Eyvallah(okay) Osman Bey.

109
00:14:35,022 --> 00:14:36,812
Eyvallah.

110
00:15:13,193 --> 00:15:15,013
Are we going to wait, my Bey?

111
00:15:20,266 --> 00:15:22,366
Bilecik Castle.

112
00:15:24,263 --> 00:15:26,853
To what do I owe this invite, Gündüz Bey?

113
00:15:28,162 --> 00:15:32,382
Do not, just do not pretend you don't
know, Lord Rogatus.

114
00:15:35,325 --> 00:15:37,525
Did you slaughter Turgut Bey's Alps?

115
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:43,000
What?

116
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:47,970
What are you talking about,
Gündüz Bey?

117
00:15:49,624 --> 00:15:51,744
You were not alone, Lord.

118
00:15:52,998 --> 00:15:54,928
You were not alone.

119
00:15:55,427 --> 00:15:58,137
Then Turgut Bey's alps...

120
00:15:58,882 --> 00:16:01,692
Now Osman Bey's horse.

121
00:16:05,702 --> 00:16:07,362
I don't get it.

122
00:16:15,532 --> 00:16:18,612
Why would I do such a thing?

123
00:16:22,487 --> 00:16:23,917
Okay.

124
00:16:23,944 --> 00:16:27,934
You'll speak to Osman Bey, not me.

125
00:16:29,677 --> 00:16:32,927
We are waiting for you in our tent
before sunset, Lord

126
00:16:58,804 --> 00:17:00,264
Boran!

127
00:17:00,488 --> 00:17:02,458
Go to Michael Kosses immediately!

128
00:17:03,066 --> 00:17:05,806
Tell him about the ambush.

129
00:17:06,638 --> 00:17:09,579
Let's see if he knows something
about this.

130
00:17:10,002 --> 00:17:11,463
Eyvallah(okay) my Bey.

131
00:17:12,773 --> 00:17:15,733
If his tongue doesn't tell...

132
00:17:17,223 --> 00:17:19,913
his hands will, his eyes will.

133
00:17:21,847 --> 00:17:23,867
Something will definitely tell it.

134
00:17:24,910 --> 00:17:26,520
Observe him well.

135
00:17:27,297 --> 00:17:28,847
Eyvallah my Bey.

136
00:17:40,628 --> 00:17:42,128
So...

137
00:17:42,693 --> 00:17:45,123
you want to become a soldier.

138
00:17:46,389 --> 00:17:48,619
- Is that right?
- Yes sir.

139
00:17:52,355 --> 00:17:53,795
Alright.

140
00:17:56,643 --> 00:18:01,313
Here is a chance for you to
show your skills.

141
00:18:05,232 --> 00:18:06,712
Attack.

142
00:18:12,098 --> 00:18:13,988
What should I do?

143
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,660
Hm?

144
00:18:15,876 --> 00:18:18,536
Should I beg you to attack me?

145
00:18:18,967 --> 00:18:20,287
Hm?

146
00:18:20,590 --> 00:18:24,740
Or should I cut your empty heads off
your worthless bodies?

147
00:18:28,127 --> 00:18:29,807
What are you looking at?

148
00:18:32,739 --> 00:18:34,149
Attack!

149
00:18:53,391 --> 00:18:56,711
- Speaking in Greek -

150
00:18:57,015 --> 00:19:02,445
Holy war wounds should always be carried
proudly.

151
00:19:05,210 --> 00:19:07,950
Take them away!
I don't want to see them.

152
00:19:08,903 --> 00:19:12,743
Train them until their
skills are observable!

153
00:19:14,094 --> 00:19:16,564
Do not be polite to them!

154
00:19:27,085 --> 00:19:30,665
As wise as he is, as sharp as his sword.
Here is my brother!

155
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:37,099
You are almighty enough to be
the Emperor of Byzantine.

156
00:19:37,799 --> 00:19:42,059
However, you let Turgut, who is a Bey
of a small tent, abduct me.

157
00:19:44,911 --> 00:19:47,491
I took my sister back at the end, right?

158
00:19:48,748 --> 00:19:50,808
Here you are.

159
00:19:51,756 --> 00:19:53,656
Yes, I am.

160
00:19:53,758 --> 00:19:56,468
But Turgut didn't pay for abducting me.

161
00:19:57,984 --> 00:20:01,254
Do not be sure about that,
my beautiful sister.

162
00:20:02,810 --> 00:20:04,230
Sir.

163
00:20:04,652 --> 00:20:07,752
- I am listening, Nesto.
- Everything goes as you wish.

164
00:20:08,347 --> 00:20:11,147
There's no sign of us.

165
00:20:11,223 --> 00:20:15,443
Moreover, everyone thinks Rogatus
killed Turgut's alps.

166
00:20:17,307 --> 00:20:20,587
You are excellent when it comes to
outsmarting your enemies, again.

167
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:25,520
Wannabe Bey paid for it by losing his alps.

168
00:20:25,937 --> 00:20:29,217
- What's more?
- You made it look like Rogatus' job.

169
00:20:30,874 --> 00:20:34,314
Your intelligence is stunning.
Here is my brother!

170
00:20:35,947 --> 00:20:38,607
Now we have a bigger problem.

171
00:20:39,326 --> 00:20:42,126
The Emperor wanted me to find Gregor.

172
00:20:42,713 --> 00:20:45,003
I am still empty-handed.

173
00:20:45,641 --> 00:20:47,401
Where do you think he is?

174
00:20:48,517 --> 00:20:50,117
Not at Rogatus.

175
00:20:50,865 --> 00:20:54,185
I am sure about that.
Catalans didn't let them act.

176
00:20:54,656 --> 00:20:57,886
What about Nicola?
Can Priest Gregor be there?

177
00:20:59,063 --> 00:21:03,083
If Nikola had the Priest, he'd
deliver him already.

178
00:21:03,433 --> 00:21:04,523
You are right.

179
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:09,175
Nikola wouldn't postpone the chance
to win Emperor's favour.

180
00:21:10,069 --> 00:21:12,859
So who has him?
Do you have someone else in mind?

181
00:21:13,662 --> 00:21:16,592
If it's not Rogatus and Nikola...

182
00:21:16,698 --> 00:21:20,008
There's only one person who can do this
around here.

183
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:23,095
That is Bey of Kayi Osman.

184
00:21:25,523 --> 00:21:27,713
Firstly, I have to be sure.

185
00:21:28,579 --> 00:21:31,019
There's only one way to be sure.

186
00:22:24,891 --> 00:22:27,396
They slaughtered Turgut Bey's alps...

187
00:22:27,396 --> 00:22:30,152
and our Bey's horse.

188
00:22:30,152 --> 00:22:33,762
We have gone through a lot, Hatuns.

189
00:22:35,166 --> 00:22:39,376
Elders say "you must be afraid of the
silent ones."

190
00:22:39,416 --> 00:22:42,226
What did they want from a sinless animal?

191
00:22:43,338 --> 00:22:45,398
They wanted to...

192
00:22:46,292 --> 00:22:48,702
threaten us, Ayse Hatun.

193
00:22:48,714 --> 00:22:52,984
Osman Bey will make them pay for sure!

194
00:22:54,822 --> 00:22:56,382
Mother!

195
00:23:00,368 --> 00:23:01,468
Sit down, daughter.

196
00:23:08,242 --> 00:23:10,302
Of course he will.

197
00:23:10,561 --> 00:23:12,231
He will.

198
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:17,160
They think they damaged my Osman.

199
00:23:17,363 --> 00:23:23,003
However, my Osman will stand up again.

200
00:23:23,130 --> 00:23:26,160
He will rear up again, Inshallah.

201
00:23:26,633 --> 00:23:28,365
He will rear up, Inshallah.

202
00:23:28,365 --> 00:23:29,235
Inshallah.

203
00:23:29,273 --> 00:23:31,273
His mother is with him now.

204
00:23:32,872 --> 00:23:37,172
Now Hatuns, it's time to get back
to work.

205
00:23:37,639 --> 00:23:42,189
Merchants of Iznik want the famous
rugs of Kayi.

206
00:23:42,642 --> 00:23:45,992
Demand is high and we have little time.

207
00:23:46,169 --> 00:23:49,829
We have to get back to work right away.

208
00:23:50,518 --> 00:23:53,308
Bala Hatun will manage it.

209
00:23:53,475 --> 00:23:58,135
As you all know, she is responsible
of the rughouse.

210
00:24:00,597 --> 00:24:02,277
The floor is yours, Bala.

211
00:24:04,530 --> 00:24:06,250
Hatuns...

212
00:24:06,630 --> 00:24:09,390
...we'll start weaving the rugs
in the morning, Inshallah.

213
00:24:09,391 --> 00:24:10,981
Inshallah.

214
00:24:11,514 --> 00:24:13,713
Gonca, take care of Hatuns.

215
00:24:13,713 --> 00:24:15,643
Don't worry Bala.

216
00:24:17,653 --> 00:24:21,023
Thank you all in advance,
skillful Hatuns of Kayi.

217
00:24:21,118 --> 00:24:24,718
The fame of our rugs is spreading
thanks to your efforts.

218
00:24:25,072 --> 00:24:27,402
- Thank you.
- Thank you Bala Hatun.

219
00:24:27,608 --> 00:24:31,908
Bala Hatun, Hatuns of Kizilcabeyogullari
are good at weaving rugs.

220
00:24:33,248 --> 00:24:37,008
Now that the demand is high
and we have little time...

221
00:24:37,359 --> 00:24:40,660
Hatuns of Kizilcabeyogullari are
ready to help.

222
00:24:40,660 --> 00:24:42,260
They are quick.

223
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:47,857
Thank you Malhun Hatun.

224
00:24:48,535 --> 00:24:50,555
It's not necessary right now.

225
00:24:52,862 --> 00:24:55,202
Kayi Hatuns overcome.

226
00:24:57,369 --> 00:24:58,576
Right, Hatuns?

227
00:24:58,576 --> 00:25:01,346
Yes, for sure, Inshallah.

228
00:25:09,226 --> 00:25:11,180
Mother Selcan, excuse me.

229
00:25:11,180 --> 00:25:13,510
Of course, daughter.

230
00:25:13,585 --> 00:25:15,225
Ayse Hatun.

231
00:25:31,826 --> 00:25:34,686
Harmanya Castle.

232
00:25:38,546 --> 00:25:41,066
Rogatus Laskaris.

233
00:25:41,458 --> 00:25:43,908
I am not surprised, to be honest!

234
00:25:44,166 --> 00:25:46,686
Only he could perform such treason!

235
00:25:50,674 --> 00:25:53,464
Maybe he wanted to kill you all there...

236
00:25:53,955 --> 00:25:56,235
and lay the blame on me.

237
00:25:57,436 --> 00:25:59,886
I am glad to see you alive.

238
00:26:00,894 --> 00:26:03,424
So are you here to inform me?

239
00:26:03,776 --> 00:26:05,976
No, Lord Kosses.

240
00:26:06,411 --> 00:26:08,941
I am here to ask by my Bey's name.

241
00:26:13,772 --> 00:26:16,262
Do you know anything about this attack?

242
00:26:21,056 --> 00:26:23,416
If I had known...

243
00:26:27,316 --> 00:26:31,266
I would have done everything I could
to prevent this.

244
00:26:32,218 --> 00:26:35,508
Send my condolences to Osman Bey, please.

245
00:26:36,636 --> 00:26:38,646
Catalans...

246
00:26:38,768 --> 00:26:40,538
are full of mercenaries.

247
00:26:41,050 --> 00:26:43,600
If I can go back to my Bey's tent
safe and sound.

248
00:26:44,201 --> 00:26:46,401
I'll surely send your condolences.

249
00:26:53,072 --> 00:26:54,812
Boran Alp.

250
00:26:59,395 --> 00:27:04,105
Don't go alone. Bithnyia is dangerous.

251
00:27:05,241 --> 00:27:09,111
Nesto, prepare a troop to
accompany Boran Alp.

252
00:27:09,235 --> 00:27:10,735
Of course.

253
00:27:41,999 --> 00:27:47,745
Allah-u Akbar
(Allah is the greatest)

254
00:27:47,745 --> 00:27:49,825
My valiant alps!

255
00:27:51,668 --> 00:27:55,918
Have you ever seen Turgut Bey not
taking revenge for his brothers?

256
00:27:56,064 --> 00:27:58,944
Have you seen him letting them down?

257
00:28:02,932 --> 00:28:04,602
Osman Bey...

258
00:28:05,135 --> 00:28:07,235
Bey of Kayi.

259
00:28:08,075 --> 00:28:10,665
He is in politics, obviously.

260
00:28:11,752 --> 00:28:13,932
He can have his own way.

261
00:28:14,034 --> 00:28:16,214
Our way is certain!

262
00:28:18,295 --> 00:28:21,885
Our brothers have been martyred by
the infidel's dirty game.

263
00:28:22,380 --> 00:28:26,090
They are treachers!
We don't even know who they are!

264
00:28:26,491 --> 00:28:31,771
If no one is guilty when we have martyrs,
that means everyone is guilty!

265
00:28:35,422 --> 00:28:39,932
Alps, we are going to take revenge
for our brothers soon.

266
00:28:40,393 --> 00:28:45,339
We are going to attack their caravans
like wolves!

267
00:28:45,339 --> 00:28:47,869
We'll destroy them!

268
00:28:51,099 --> 00:28:56,069
We shall mourn till sunrise.

269
00:28:57,671 --> 00:29:01,961
We shall mourn so that sun rises
for our revenge!

270
00:29:02,467 --> 00:29:08,527
Allah-u Akbar
(Allah is the greatest)

271
00:30:19,487 --> 00:30:20,857
Boran.

272
00:30:21,575 --> 00:30:22,895
Yes my Bey.

273
00:30:26,130 --> 00:30:30,100
Things are unclear.

274
00:30:31,442 --> 00:30:36,702
The only thing I am sure is that
Kosses cut alps' fingers.

275
00:30:39,346 --> 00:30:41,426
Do not go alone.

276
00:30:42,113 --> 00:30:47,123
Take some soldiers with you while leaving
Armankaya.

277
00:30:50,225 --> 00:30:54,115
As you know, things are unclear.

278
00:30:56,337 --> 00:30:58,337
Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.

279
00:31:09,774 --> 00:31:12,004
Don't do it.
Leave us alone.

280
00:31:17,124 --> 00:31:18,534
Have mercy!

281
00:31:43,190 --> 00:31:47,790
My Bey, you promised that my father
would return.

282
00:31:48,208 --> 00:31:52,438
They martyred him,
also they cut his fingers!

283
00:31:53,011 --> 00:31:54,871
You promised.

284
00:31:58,740 --> 00:32:00,550
A finger for a finger.

285
00:33:10,211 --> 00:33:13,111
Now go to your Lord Michael Kosses.

286
00:33:15,650 --> 00:33:19,460
This is for the cut fingers
of Turgut Bey's alps.

287
00:33:21,920 --> 00:33:24,900
If I could have him here...

288
00:33:26,975 --> 00:33:30,205
He would paid for this.

289
00:33:32,836 --> 00:33:34,396
Let's go.

290
00:34:11,303 --> 00:34:13,413
Bala Hatun forgot that we are the
Hatuns of this tent too...

291
00:34:13,565 --> 00:34:17,005
just because we stayed in
for forty days.

292
00:34:19,331 --> 00:34:23,462
It's time to remind the ones who forgot
that we are here.

293
00:34:26,117 --> 00:34:27,735
Gokce...

294
00:34:27,735 --> 00:34:30,016
I wish you to be responsible for this.

295
00:34:30,264 --> 00:34:36,105
Go to Kizilcabey Tent quickly. Bring the
most skillful Hatuns to weave rugs.

296
00:34:39,739 --> 00:34:41,650
As you order, Malhun Hatun.

297
00:34:41,650 --> 00:34:42,960
But...

298
00:34:44,672 --> 00:34:47,793
Selcan Hatun held responsible Bala Hatun
on this job.

299
00:34:48,578 --> 00:34:51,188
Bala Hatun didn't want our Hatun.

300
00:34:51,245 --> 00:34:52,676
How will she react?

301
00:34:52,676 --> 00:34:55,156
It's too late, Gokce.

302
00:34:55,214 --> 00:34:58,654
Bala Hatun can't see things coming.
She won't make it by time.

303
00:34:59,646 --> 00:35:02,656
Also, we are not doing anything wrong.

304
00:35:02,740 --> 00:35:05,150
We want to help.
They reject our help.

305
00:35:05,384 --> 00:35:07,324
Now go fetch the Hatuns.

306
00:35:11,616 --> 00:35:13,906
If we manage to do this job...

307
00:35:14,096 --> 00:35:16,416
we will gain dignity here.

308
00:35:18,809 --> 00:35:22,399
Gokce, I want something else from you.

309
00:35:23,506 --> 00:35:26,906
Leave your two most trusted Hatuns
with my Orhan.

310
00:35:28,056 --> 00:35:30,346
They must stay in the tent all the time.

311
00:35:31,041 --> 00:35:33,231
It's dangerous out here nowadays.

312
00:35:34,081 --> 00:35:35,631
Do not worry.

313
00:36:00,222 --> 00:36:02,132
He says he didn't do it.

314
00:36:03,104 --> 00:36:05,124
He says he knows neither about Alps...

315
00:36:07,299 --> 00:36:09,519
nor about the horse.

316
00:36:12,230 --> 00:36:14,430
What do you think, brother?

317
00:36:15,536 --> 00:36:18,146
How did he react when he saw you?

318
00:36:19,207 --> 00:36:23,727
A part of me says
"it's obvious, it must be Rogatus."

319
00:36:26,433 --> 00:36:28,563
The other part of me says...

320
00:36:31,295 --> 00:36:34,515
I don't know, I am not sure as well,
Osman Bey.

321
00:36:39,685 --> 00:36:42,445
He was like hearing it for the first time
when we talked.

322
00:36:45,052 --> 00:36:48,222
However, he wants Gregor the most.

323
00:36:52,523 --> 00:36:54,143
I don't know.

324
00:36:56,035 --> 00:36:57,905
We'll figure it out, brother.

325
00:36:58,909 --> 00:37:01,309
Once he arrives in our tent...

326
00:37:01,739 --> 00:37:03,999
Once he faces us...

327
00:37:05,153 --> 00:37:06,953
...then we'll understand.

328
00:37:29,641 --> 00:37:31,051
Any trace yet?

329
00:37:36,304 --> 00:37:37,954
No, my bey.

330
00:37:43,030 --> 00:37:44,960
We searched everywhere.

331
00:37:45,078 --> 00:37:47,668
There isn't a single spot that
we didn't check.

332
00:37:48,844 --> 00:37:49,974
But...

333
00:37:52,361 --> 00:37:53,771
no...

334
00:37:56,356 --> 00:37:58,956
but we'll find it.

335
00:38:00,020 --> 00:38:01,850
Inshallah.

336
00:38:30,129 --> 00:38:33,179
Harmankaya Castle

337
00:38:59,187 --> 00:39:01,607
You need to taste this.

338
00:39:09,197 --> 00:39:11,083
It's delicious.

339
00:39:11,083 --> 00:39:13,583
But it's enough for now.

340
00:39:14,091 --> 00:39:17,531
Because I want you to preserve
your hunger until the meat.

341
00:39:20,394 --> 00:39:24,184
You know, not every chief can spread
the meat...

342
00:39:24,848 --> 00:39:27,558
from its bones.

343
00:39:32,913 --> 00:39:35,883
It should be done with dexterity.

344
00:39:36,115 --> 00:39:38,405
Never tore it apart.

345
00:39:38,405 --> 00:39:40,205
Or else it won't be delicious.

346
00:40:00,838 --> 00:40:02,738
Allow me, brother.

347
00:40:03,866 --> 00:40:05,236
Look.

348
00:40:08,061 --> 00:40:10,301
There is a nerve here.

349
00:40:11,674 --> 00:40:13,684
Here is my sister.

350
00:40:13,874 --> 00:40:18,254
She sees what others can't,
and she takes care of it.

351
00:40:19,345 --> 00:40:21,175
You were always like this.

352
00:40:21,473 --> 00:40:23,873
Smart and dangerous.

353
00:40:26,099 --> 00:40:27,999
Osman's envoy.

354
00:40:28,176 --> 00:40:30,886
The bey of the Kayı must
have doubts about you.

355
00:40:31,493 --> 00:40:34,883
I think your plans about Rogatus
isn't going well.

356
00:40:35,054 --> 00:40:39,934
Cooking is like a game
with rules, Mari.

357
00:40:40,482 --> 00:40:43,112
If you don't follow to rules...

358
00:40:43,781 --> 00:40:45,661
your meal won't be tasty.

359
00:40:50,170 --> 00:40:51,850
Yes.

360
00:40:52,806 --> 00:40:54,516
Yes.

361
00:40:54,749 --> 00:40:57,419
We spread it.

362
00:41:04,777 --> 00:41:06,367
Like I said...

363
00:41:06,708 --> 00:41:09,318
cooking is a matter of patience.

364
00:41:10,633 --> 00:41:14,153
You should believe in your brother.

365
00:41:15,803 --> 00:41:18,503
You know that I always believe in you.

366
00:41:18,800 --> 00:41:22,650
Come on, then. Help me.
So we can begin.

367
00:41:23,673 --> 00:41:27,163
We don't want Aya Nikola to be
left hungry, right?

368
00:41:28,111 --> 00:41:30,791
Of course, we don't.

369
00:41:33,853 --> 00:41:35,293
My lord.

370
00:41:37,089 --> 00:41:39,119
There is something important.

371
00:41:39,567 --> 00:41:40,887
Osman.

372
00:41:41,285 --> 00:41:43,925
He cut our soldiers' fingers.

373
00:41:52,777 --> 00:41:55,587
If he stopped at the fingers...

374
00:41:55,638 --> 00:41:58,438
he's also suspicious of Rogatus.

375
00:41:58,482 --> 00:42:00,762
So, he doesn't think we are responsible.

376
00:42:03,793 --> 00:42:09,113
When you said important, I thought
it was about Father Gregor.

377
00:42:10,668 --> 00:42:13,678
There isn't anything new about
Father Gregor yet, my lord.

378
00:42:18,098 --> 00:42:20,138
Of course not!

379
00:42:20,384 --> 00:42:23,384
Nothing can happen with the likes of you!

380
00:42:24,349 --> 00:42:25,759
Get out!

381
00:42:43,652 --> 00:42:47,232
You, my Karayel,
my companion for life...

382
00:42:48,688 --> 00:42:51,168
you accompanied me
for so many years.

383
00:42:52,029 --> 00:42:55,659
You carried me when I was
young and inexperienced.

384
00:42:56,096 --> 00:43:00,946
You were bled but you ran into
battles without stopping.

385
00:43:01,506 --> 00:43:03,536
I owe you my life.

386
00:43:03,651 --> 00:43:07,781
My noble Karayel, you were
a witness to my joy...

387
00:43:08,408 --> 00:43:13,028
anger, and oaths...

388
00:43:25,906 --> 00:43:28,506
I swear to Allah...

389
00:43:31,133 --> 00:43:34,183
those who ripped off my wings...

390
00:43:35,785 --> 00:43:37,105
Karayel!

391
00:43:39,904 --> 00:43:42,154
those who took you from me...

392
00:43:42,676 --> 00:43:49,396
will be crushed under the shoes of
many noble horses like you.

393
00:43:53,302 --> 00:43:55,302
I take an oath...

394
00:43:56,220 --> 00:43:58,900
I won't let your blood on the ground!

395
00:44:05,391 --> 00:44:07,791
Be my witness, my father...

396
00:44:10,704 --> 00:44:13,044
be my witness, my Allah...

397
00:44:21,248 --> 00:44:23,858
Harmankaya Castle

398
00:44:26,577 --> 00:44:28,507
My dear friend...

399
00:44:29,403 --> 00:44:34,803
when I was equipping my soldiers with
Rogatus's shields to send them to Osman...

400
00:44:35,752 --> 00:44:38,642
you did a great job.

401
00:44:39,617 --> 00:44:44,147
You killed Osman's well-loved horse.

402
00:44:44,779 --> 00:44:47,689
Ripping his head off?

403
00:44:56,963 --> 00:45:00,453
You are really merciless, you know that?

404
00:45:01,965 --> 00:45:04,178
You are a real Turk.

405
00:45:04,178 --> 00:45:09,688
I'm sure when Osman finds out what
happened, he was frustrated.

406
00:45:10,413 --> 00:45:12,043
What do you say?

407
00:45:13,103 --> 00:45:17,543
I've only done the job you asked,
Lord Kosses.

408
00:45:17,594 --> 00:45:20,867
-We did our job.
-You did well, Bahadır.

409
00:45:20,867 --> 00:45:24,827
We increased the number of alps
around the tribe as you want, my bey.

410
00:45:24,971 --> 00:45:27,641
-Keep your eyes open.
-Don't worry, my bey.

411
00:45:29,967 --> 00:45:32,237
Your new job is much more important.

412
00:45:32,410 --> 00:45:33,976
Father Gregor.

413
00:45:33,976 --> 00:45:36,176
I think he's in Osman's hands.

414
00:45:36,639 --> 00:45:40,699
Is there anything that you noticed
in the tribe?

415
00:45:43,143 --> 00:45:45,661
I'm not sure if it's Gregor or not but...

416
00:45:45,661 --> 00:45:49,481
I know that something is being kept
hidden in that tent.

417
00:45:51,173 --> 00:45:53,593
Is that so?

418
00:45:54,410 --> 00:45:57,430
They don't let anyone in but
Osman's loyal alps.

419
00:45:58,098 --> 00:46:02,648
And no one leaves the tent. Nobody
knows what's inside.

420
00:46:05,011 --> 00:46:08,181
You'll find out who is inside
that tent, Bahadır.

421
00:46:09,866 --> 00:46:12,506
My feelings never deceived me.

422
00:46:13,248 --> 00:46:16,778
I feel that we are getting closer
to Gregor.

423
00:46:17,394 --> 00:46:20,746
We are so close, Bahadır.
So close.

424
00:46:49,768 --> 00:46:52,518
Bala Hatun, be careful.

425
00:46:53,174 --> 00:46:55,698
Now you carry two lives.

426
00:46:55,698 --> 00:46:58,008
You need to sit and rest.

427
00:47:22,875 --> 00:47:24,725
Gündüz.

428
00:47:30,142 --> 00:47:32,232
Gündüz.

429
00:47:32,496 --> 00:47:33,893
Mother.

430
00:47:33,893 --> 00:47:37,183
Where is Osman?
Isn't he here yet?

431
00:47:38,997 --> 00:47:43,757
What should he do, mother? We let
our brother down.

432
00:47:45,344 --> 00:47:47,254
What should he do?

433
00:47:49,007 --> 00:47:51,367
He wants to stay alone.

434
00:47:58,864 --> 00:48:00,724
Sit.

435
00:48:05,877 --> 00:48:07,497
Welcome.

436
00:48:12,822 --> 00:48:14,362
Are you alright?

437
00:48:20,531 --> 00:48:23,061
With the name of Allah.

438
00:48:25,437 --> 00:48:27,177
Enjoy your meal.

439
00:48:44,202 --> 00:48:46,542
Anything new, brother?

440
00:48:46,831 --> 00:48:48,681
No, Osman Bey.

441
00:48:49,004 --> 00:48:52,364
Alps are still searching. They must've
left a trace.

442
00:48:54,320 --> 00:48:55,990
We'll find it.

443
00:48:58,764 --> 00:48:59,924
Inshallah.

444
00:49:04,714 --> 00:49:08,204
I don't think they can enter when
there are so many alps, my bey.

445
00:49:08,834 --> 00:49:10,964
You are right.

446
00:49:12,867 --> 00:49:15,697
But it wasn't someone from inside.

447
00:49:16,324 --> 00:49:18,784
How did they do it then, mother?

448
00:49:18,789 --> 00:49:22,779
It's not someone from inside but
they can't enter either.

449
00:49:24,453 --> 00:49:26,503
It must be someone who can
enter freely.

450
00:49:27,354 --> 00:49:30,724
We do trade and host guests.

451
00:49:31,655 --> 00:49:33,605
So many people enter and leave.

452
00:49:42,226 --> 00:49:44,626
Thank Allah for today.

453
00:49:46,758 --> 00:49:51,608
We passed many trials and
had many casualties.

454
00:49:52,350 --> 00:49:56,510
But today, we are at this table again.

455
00:49:58,055 --> 00:50:05,215
Thank Allah for gathering us around
this table.

456
00:50:05,971 --> 00:50:07,671
Amin.

457
00:50:08,244 --> 00:50:10,694
-Amin.
-Amin.

458
00:50:13,403 --> 00:50:15,483
I should take a rest.

459
00:50:21,155 --> 00:50:22,845
Enjoy your meal.

460
00:50:47,229 --> 00:50:49,749
Harmankaya Castle

461
00:50:50,922 --> 00:50:52,452
Mari.

462
00:50:55,439 --> 00:50:58,739
If your eyes weren't shining
like a gem...

463
00:50:59,732 --> 00:51:02,772
I was nearly forgetting about
the gift I bought for you.

464
00:51:17,130 --> 00:51:18,920
Glamorous.

465
00:51:19,886 --> 00:51:21,986
I hope you like it.

466
00:51:28,786 --> 00:51:30,666
If you allow me.

467
00:51:53,736 --> 00:51:56,636
I really liked it, Aya Nikola.
Thank you.

468
00:51:57,699 --> 00:52:03,889
I've never met anyone better at
making their friends pleased, Nikola.

469
00:52:07,202 --> 00:52:11,202
I like this gentle act from Aya Nikola,
brother.

470
00:52:11,692 --> 00:52:16,152
But I've never been a woman who is
easy to please.

471
00:52:16,247 --> 00:52:18,407
You know it.

472
00:52:31,706 --> 00:52:36,266
What should I do to please you,
Dear Mari?

473
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:45,600
Do you know what is the thing that
impressed me the most about you?

474
00:52:45,600 --> 00:52:47,910
I'm curious.

475
00:52:48,153 --> 00:52:52,903
You change the lives of those
who hurt your friends.

476
00:52:53,128 --> 00:52:57,758
Mari, if you want it...

477
00:52:57,758 --> 00:53:01,758
I can change the world even.

478
00:53:03,235 --> 00:53:08,365
-You must know the Turk who kidnapped me--
-Turgut.

479
00:53:08,693 --> 00:53:12,053
Yes, Turgut.

480
00:53:12,972 --> 00:53:16,972
-Will he get away with this--
-He won't.

481
00:53:19,342 --> 00:53:22,852
I promise you, Mari, he won't.

482
00:53:22,852 --> 00:53:27,342
So, I'll start changing the world
from Turgut.

483
00:53:36,458 --> 00:53:39,628
-Nikola.
-Rogatus.

484
00:53:39,628 --> 00:53:42,898
I'm glad you are here too.

485
00:53:43,464 --> 00:53:47,464
There are important matters I want to
talk about.

486
00:53:48,780 --> 00:53:52,780
What a surprise!

487
00:54:16,913 --> 00:54:20,913
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come, mother.

488
00:54:21,742 --> 00:54:24,722
Come.

489
00:54:28,322 --> 00:54:31,022
Come.

490
00:54:38,088 --> 00:54:43,458
You were just like this when you were
a child and sad. You would be alone.

491
00:54:46,432 --> 00:54:50,432
And you would understand me and
come to me.

492
00:54:51,045 --> 00:54:56,575
You would cure my motherlessness.
How can I repay you, mother?

493
00:54:56,675 --> 00:54:59,955
What payment between a mother
and a son, son?

494
00:54:59,955 --> 00:55:05,445
I cured your motherlessness and
you cured my grief of losing a child.

495
00:55:07,503 --> 00:55:11,503
We cured each other's wounds.

496
00:55:14,752 --> 00:55:18,752
Get yourself together now.

497
00:55:18,752 --> 00:55:22,752
Does it fit Osman Bey to be like this?

498
00:55:23,521 --> 00:55:26,761
It's heavy, mother.

499
00:55:27,838 --> 00:55:31,568
We've shown weakness.

500
00:55:33,814 --> 00:55:38,324
We couldn't protect what we were
responsible of.

501
00:55:38,936 --> 00:55:42,936
They killed Turgut Bey's alps first.

502
00:55:42,936 --> 00:55:48,416
Then, the enemy sneaked into the
tribe and took my Karayel.

503
00:55:49,887 --> 00:55:53,887
-Isn't this weakness, mother?
-Not at all!

504
00:55:53,887 --> 00:55:58,827
What are you saying, son?
You are too hard on yourself.

505
00:55:59,690 --> 00:56:04,690
Look, son. The mountain's burden
is as heavy as the mountain.

506
00:56:04,828 --> 00:56:08,828
You made all heathens kneel.

507
00:56:08,828 --> 00:56:14,118
They act behind you because
they can't face you.

508
00:56:15,858 --> 00:56:19,858
You will overcome this too.

509
00:56:20,031 --> 00:56:25,471
There is a saying, Allah gives us burdens
as heavy as we can carry.

510
00:56:29,022 --> 00:56:33,022
May Allah give you heavy burdens.

511
00:56:33,902 --> 00:56:37,902
Amin, mother. Amin.

512
00:56:38,884 --> 00:56:42,884
I should leave so you can rest.

513
00:56:43,694 --> 00:56:49,434
After all these words, it's not good
to sit. There is much to do, mother.

514
00:56:49,860 --> 00:56:53,860
Mashallah.

515
00:56:54,499 --> 00:56:59,779
So, Osman accused me of killing
Turgut's alps.

516
00:57:03,602 --> 00:57:07,602
Is there anything you want
to say about this, Kosses.

517
00:57:08,662 --> 00:57:12,662
Osman told me about his suspicion
of you.

518
00:57:13,783 --> 00:57:17,783
I told him how baseless his
suspicion was.

519
00:57:17,783 --> 00:57:21,783
I hope the truth will be revealed soon,
my friend.

520
00:57:21,952 --> 00:57:26,592
Whether you hope or not, I'll reveal it.

521
00:57:35,873 --> 00:57:40,833
Rogatus, you didn't lead
that attack, did you?

522
00:57:42,722 --> 00:57:47,462
You are with friends, you don't need
to hide it.

523
00:57:47,539 --> 00:57:51,539
I'm with friends.

524
00:57:53,606 --> 00:57:57,606
Do you think the same, Kosses?

525
00:57:58,163 --> 00:58:01,283
That I'm with friends?

526
00:58:01,283 --> 00:58:06,163
If you doubt it, don't you think
it's weird to be at our table?

527
00:58:08,703 --> 00:58:12,703
-I can leave if I disturb you--
-Rogatus.

528
00:58:14,714 --> 00:58:19,144
Will we stab each other instead
of building an alliance?

529
00:58:19,144 --> 00:58:23,144
-You are being resentful.
-You are calling me resentful...

530
00:58:23,144 --> 00:58:27,144
while someone is trying to
feed me to Osman, Nikola.

531
00:58:30,964 --> 00:58:35,824
And also, I wasn't
only accused of killing the Alps...

532
00:58:35,824 --> 00:58:41,214
but also killing Osman's horse!

533
00:58:42,593 --> 00:58:47,553
Osman's horse is killed?
That's a pity.

534
00:58:51,390 --> 00:58:56,030
Someone crossed the line, huh?

535
00:58:59,837 --> 00:59:03,837
Whatever, we have more important
problems...

536
00:59:03,837 --> 00:59:09,237
in Bhytinia. I can't mourn for
Osman's horse now.

537
00:59:13,761 --> 00:59:19,141
Father Gregor is still missing.
Are you aware of that?

538
00:59:19,294 --> 00:59:24,114
Where did that man go?
Underground?

539
00:59:24,114 --> 00:59:29,194
He is a priest, Nikola.
Maybe he ascended.

540
00:59:36,059 --> 00:59:39,849
Father Gregor...

541
00:59:40,988 --> 00:59:44,388
is a respectable reverend.

542
00:59:44,388 --> 00:59:48,988
I assume the emperor
doesn't have the same feelings.

543
00:59:59,764 --> 01:00:06,274
I said it before. I don't think anyone
here has Father Gregor. I'm sure of it.

544
01:00:09,606 --> 01:00:14,626
But Osman...
I'm not sure.

545
01:00:17,775 --> 01:00:21,775
I'm not sure who has him.

546
01:00:21,775 --> 01:00:25,775
But I agree with you about
none of us having him, Nikola.

547
01:00:27,003 --> 01:00:31,633
What do you think, Dear Rogatus?

548
01:00:34,189 --> 01:00:38,189
In Bhytinia...

549
01:00:40,074 --> 01:00:44,074
we can't be sure of anyone
or anything.

550
01:00:45,383 --> 01:00:49,383
That's the only thing I think of.

551
01:00:57,484 --> 01:01:00,814
It was delicious.

552
01:01:02,516 --> 01:01:07,486
Unfortunately, I have to go.
Until next time.

553
01:01:38,029 --> 01:01:42,819
Master Gregor, we must take it
out of your arm at once.

554
01:01:42,819 --> 01:01:46,969
-Your wound is getting worse.
-Not before escaping, Andreas.

555
01:01:47,793 --> 01:01:51,223
We can't take it before assuring
our security.

556
01:01:51,223 --> 01:01:55,793
We don't know when this captivity
will end, Master Gregor.

557
01:01:55,885 --> 01:01:59,885
It looks like we'll stay
here for a while.

558
01:02:00,800 --> 01:02:04,800
Osman has alps everywhere.

559
01:02:04,800 --> 01:02:09,580
-We can't inform Rogatus.
-You are mistaken, Andreas.

560
01:02:10,309 --> 01:02:14,309
Osman is a smart man.

561
01:02:14,309 --> 01:02:18,999
He didn't kidnap us to hide us.
He knows the emperor's politics...

562
01:02:18,999 --> 01:02:24,129
and the weaknesses of Byzantine.
-He must've planned his moves.

563
01:02:24,129 --> 01:02:26,999
That's why he kidnapped us.

564
01:02:26,999 --> 01:02:32,569
He wants to work up the fight between
the Catholics and the Orthodoxes.

565
01:02:32,867 --> 01:02:37,617
So, keeping us here won't benefit him.

566
01:02:37,717 --> 01:02:42,707
Osman's politics will take us to Rogatus,
Andreas.

567
01:03:05,430 --> 01:03:09,430
Osman Bey, it's time.

568
01:03:09,684 --> 01:03:13,794
It's getting dark.
Rogatus isn't coming.

569
01:03:14,630 --> 01:03:18,310
We know our enemy now, huh?

570
01:03:18,310 --> 01:03:22,630
You are right.

571
01:03:22,630 --> 01:03:27,380
By not attending to our invitation,
Rogatus gets suspicious.

572
01:03:29,254 --> 01:03:33,984
If he isn't coming, we'll go to him.

573
01:03:35,439 --> 01:03:39,819
Then, we'll understand if
it's fear...

574
01:03:40,844 --> 01:03:44,844
or guiltyness.
-Then, if you allow me.

575
01:03:45,861 --> 01:03:49,861
Wait, brother.

576
01:03:54,545 --> 01:03:58,545
Tell me, my bey.

577
01:03:58,820 --> 01:04:02,140
Will you judge me?

578
01:04:04,350 --> 01:04:08,350
It's not the day for judgement.

579
01:04:11,245 --> 01:04:14,875
It's the day for unity.

580
01:04:16,488 --> 01:04:19,968
I don't want to ride alone.

581
01:04:19,968 --> 01:04:25,618
Redemption of mistakes is possible
by unity, right, my bey?

582
01:04:25,618 --> 01:04:28,618
Indeed.

583
01:04:45,041 --> 01:04:49,831
-Aya Nikola is tasteful.
-He is.

584
01:04:50,554 --> 01:04:54,554
But he is ready to fall into
a trap, like all men.

585
01:04:54,683 --> 01:04:58,683
You should've seen him looking
into my eyes.

586
01:04:58,849 --> 01:05:02,379
I'm sure he fell in love with
you at first sight.

587
01:05:02,379 --> 01:05:06,399
It was so obvious.

588
01:05:06,663 --> 01:05:11,543
I can't even imagine what he'll
do to Turgut for kidnapping me.

589
01:05:20,325 --> 01:05:22,795
My lady...

590
01:05:24,773 --> 01:05:30,323
-I want to ask you if you allow me.
-Of course, ask away.

591
01:05:31,294 --> 01:05:36,424
But wait! You wonder what I want
from Nikola, right?

592
01:05:38,392 --> 01:05:42,882
What I want from the others.
His power.

593
01:05:46,751 --> 01:05:50,751
I'll play with him for a while.

594
01:05:50,751 --> 01:05:53,651
Then I'll move him like a puppet.

595
01:05:54,732 --> 01:05:58,732
A puppet that will do whatever I want.

596
01:05:59,635 --> 01:06:03,145
You may leave.

597
01:06:08,034 --> 01:06:11,294
Poor Turgut.

598
01:06:11,294 --> 01:06:16,034
You'll pay the price for kidnapping me,
just like your alps.

599
01:06:31,093 --> 01:06:34,783
-Any news from Rogatus?
-No, brother.

600
01:06:34,783 --> 01:06:38,223
Then, we'll go.

601
01:06:38,223 --> 01:06:40,233
Alps!

602
01:06:53,778 --> 01:06:57,108
Kosses.

603
01:07:00,633 --> 01:07:04,903
He wouldn't come without telling.
It must be important.

604
01:07:04,903 --> 01:07:09,653
He must've come here for his
soldiers' fingers.

605
01:07:11,723 --> 01:07:14,523
Clear the way!

606
01:07:15,869 --> 01:07:19,739
Kosses' soldiers are here, my bey.

607
01:07:41,406 --> 01:07:46,016
Where is Lord Kosses?
Why did he send you here?

608
01:07:47,691 --> 01:07:52,571
Haven't you heard? Are you deaf
or mute?

609
01:08:01,050 --> 01:08:04,000
Rogatus?

610
01:08:09,240 --> 01:08:14,700
You invited me and I'm here.
Why are you surprised, Osman Bey?

611
01:08:32,322 --> 01:08:36,322
Turn to your jobs, women.
Come on.

612
01:08:46,557 --> 01:08:49,327
What's happening here?

613
01:08:52,060 --> 01:08:56,880
-Who are you, women?
-Kızılcabeyoğlu's women, Gonca Hatun.

614
01:08:59,102 --> 01:09:03,752
-They are here for work.
-What are you saying, Gökçe?

615
01:09:05,171 --> 01:09:09,821
Look at me, woman!
You are stepping over your limit.

616
01:09:10,587 --> 01:09:17,227
Bala Hatun didn't allow this. How can
you bring them here?

617
01:09:17,227 --> 01:09:21,657
It's Malhun Hatun's orders,
not mine.

618
01:09:21,657 --> 01:09:26,537
-Speak to her.
-Bala Hatun makes the decisions.

619
01:09:26,703 --> 01:09:30,698
She is in charge of here!

620
01:09:30,698 --> 01:09:35,178
She answered Malhun Hatun's
question as you heard.

621
01:09:36,294 --> 01:09:41,764
Now, tell the women to return
to their tribe.

622
01:09:42,352 --> 01:09:46,352
The workers are behind me.

623
01:09:50,745 --> 01:09:54,115
Gonca Hatun.

624
01:09:58,895 --> 01:10:02,895
Gökçe and the women are here
by my order.

625
01:10:04,410 --> 01:10:08,410
Speak to me if you have objections.

626
01:10:19,003 --> 01:10:23,003
-Give me patience...
-Power to your elbows, women.

627
01:10:23,008 --> 01:10:27,008
Make me proud.

628
01:10:30,202 --> 01:10:34,542
What's wrong, Gonca? Why are you
waiting here like this?

629
01:10:34,542 --> 01:10:39,762
Malhun Hatun brought women from her
tribe to work here.

630
01:10:45,286 --> 01:10:49,286
And put Gökçe in charge.

631
01:10:52,016 --> 01:10:55,336
What should we do now, Bala Hatun?

632
01:11:05,261 --> 01:11:09,261
Bilecik is known by its workmen,
Osman Bey.

633
01:11:09,261 --> 01:11:13,261
They can make the same shields that
Harmankaya soldiers hold.

634
01:11:14,011 --> 01:11:18,661
That's the kind of trap Kosses
made for you. Don't fall for it.

635
01:11:24,369 --> 01:11:29,199
If I had ordered my soldiers
to attack your tribe...

636
01:11:29,199 --> 01:11:32,899
wouldn't you think that it was Kosses?

637
01:11:34,500 --> 01:11:38,500
I wouldn't, Rogatus.

638
01:11:40,844 --> 01:11:44,844
But there is no need for such
exhibitions.

639
01:11:45,089 --> 01:11:49,089
If I was sure of your treachery...

640
01:11:51,727 --> 01:11:55,727
you wouldn't be here talking to me.

641
01:11:57,424 --> 01:12:01,424
What about Gündüz Bey's invitation?

642
01:12:03,293 --> 01:12:07,823
I thought you were deceived
by Kosses.

643
01:12:08,290 --> 01:12:14,330
Despite all our trade and friendship--

644
01:12:14,330 --> 01:12:18,330
I'm Ertuğrul Ghazi's son, Osman Bey.

645
01:12:20,424 --> 01:12:24,424
I know well about your schemes.

646
01:12:28,356 --> 01:12:32,356
But the truth has a tendency...

647
01:12:32,356 --> 01:12:36,356
to get revealed sooner or later.

648
01:12:40,693 --> 01:12:45,023
Sheik Edebali wanted to
send the workers of your tribe...

649
01:12:45,023 --> 01:12:49,607
to learn mining at my
silver mines, and I accept it.

650
01:12:49,986 --> 01:12:54,086
I'm providing many goods from you,
instead of buying them cheaper.

651
01:12:54,086 --> 01:12:58,086
These are not hostile attitudes,
Osman Bey.

652
01:12:58,502 --> 01:13:03,062
And I want the truth to be revealed
as much as you do.

653
01:13:03,742 --> 01:13:07,232
Until next time.

654
01:13:26,952 --> 01:13:30,952
Everything got more complicated, brother.

655
01:13:30,952 --> 01:13:34,722
Indeed, brother.
Indeed.

656
01:13:34,908 --> 01:13:40,018
But, we know one thing...

657
01:13:43,987 --> 01:13:47,987
all traces are leading to
the same direction.

658
01:13:52,582 --> 01:13:57,742
Whoever wants Gregor is doing this.

659
01:13:57,742 --> 01:14:01,742
You are right, Osman.

660
01:14:01,742 --> 01:14:05,942
Kosses, Nikola, Rogatus and
even the Emperor.

661
01:14:06,146 --> 01:14:10,146
They all want the priest.
Don't worry.

662
01:14:10,146 --> 01:14:14,146
-We'll increase the caution.
-No.

663
01:14:14,665 --> 01:14:18,415
The opposite, brother.

664
01:14:19,398 --> 01:14:23,398
We'll take Priest Gregor
out of the tribe.

665
01:14:23,398 --> 01:14:28,188
Whoever wants him will use
this opportunity.

666
01:14:29,530 --> 01:14:33,530
Then, we'll know who is the enemy.

667
01:14:36,399 --> 01:14:40,399
Inshallah, Osman Bey.
Inshallah.

668
01:14:42,634 --> 01:14:47,604
Now, let's take the good news
to Priest Gregor.

669
01:15:08,050 --> 01:15:11,690
Malhun Hatun, good day.

670
01:15:13,993 --> 01:15:17,103
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

671
01:15:18,777 --> 01:15:22,777
Malhun Hatun, haven't we
talked about this?

672
01:15:22,777 --> 01:15:26,327
Haven't I told you that there is no need?
What is this?

673
01:15:26,327 --> 01:15:30,117
You are right, Bala Hatun.
We have.

674
01:15:30,117 --> 01:15:34,327
But you forget one thing. I'm also
a Hatun of this tribe.

675
01:15:35,671 --> 01:15:40,441
I don't need orders to
do something.

676
01:15:43,850 --> 01:15:48,200
Of course, you are a Hatun of
this tribe.

677
01:15:48,404 --> 01:15:53,004
But I'm the Head Hatun of this tribe.

678
01:16:01,680 --> 01:16:06,820
When everyone does as they wish,
there can be no unity.

679
01:16:06,820 --> 01:16:09,680
The tribe has an order.

680
01:16:09,680 --> 01:16:14,510
Bala Hatun, you are forgetting
another thing.

681
01:16:15,666 --> 01:16:18,826
I'm a bey's daughter.

682
01:16:18,826 --> 01:16:22,826
I have no lessons to take from you
about administration.

683
01:16:25,321 --> 01:16:30,211
My intentions are sincere. There is
little time. We want to help.

684
01:16:30,454 --> 01:16:35,114
This much job can't be done with
Kayı' women only.

685
01:16:41,572 --> 01:16:46,152
Come on, women. Get to your
job.

686
01:16:46,152 --> 01:16:50,482
-Our carpets are on your hands now.
-Thank you, Bala Hatun.

687
01:17:15,509 --> 01:17:18,019
Ahmet.

688
01:17:27,135 --> 01:17:31,585
May Allah give strength to your elbows.

689
01:17:31,585 --> 01:17:35,025
May Allah help you.

690
01:17:35,025 --> 01:17:39,565
-May your job be finished in no time.
-Thank you, Ahmet.

691
01:17:39,832 --> 01:17:43,832
So, the Kayı's most overhasty alp
wished you his best.

692
01:17:43,832 --> 01:17:47,312
-Inshallah it'll be finished soon.
-Inshallah.

693
01:17:52,156 --> 01:17:56,156
Kill our enemies for the sake of
your love.

694
01:17:56,156 --> 01:18:00,156
Destroy all our enemies because
we are your followers.

695
01:18:00,156 --> 01:18:05,226
Our God Jesus Christ,
save us with your mercy.

696
01:18:05,399 --> 01:18:07,949
Amen.

697
01:18:11,430 --> 01:18:16,930
-Finish your prayer. Don't mind us.
-We don't. It was finished.

698
01:18:26,793 --> 01:18:30,635
I say that, Priest Gregor...

699
01:18:30,635 --> 01:18:36,705
you will do your worships in the church
in Söğüt, freely.

700
01:18:40,537 --> 01:18:43,847
Don't be surprised.

701
01:18:43,847 --> 01:18:50,177
Our Prophet, praise be upon him,
used to do that.

702
01:18:51,333 --> 01:18:55,903
No non-muslim would get hurt...

703
01:18:55,903 --> 01:19:00,983
or be disturbed during their prayers,
under his rule.

704
01:19:02,806 --> 01:19:07,526
-I follow his way.
-Are you doing that by keeping us captive?

705
01:19:08,058 --> 01:19:12,658
You aren't captives here.
You are our guests.

706
01:19:13,591 --> 01:19:17,591
We keep you here to protect
your lives.

707
01:19:17,839 --> 01:19:21,839
I care about your worship as much
as...

708
01:19:21,839 --> 01:19:25,839
I care about my Christian people at Söğüt.

709
01:19:27,879 --> 01:19:31,509
My Alps will take you to Söğüt.

710
01:19:41,534 --> 01:19:44,404
-Göktuğ, Saltuk.
-My bey.

711
01:19:44,404 --> 01:19:47,944
-You will take Priest Gregor.
-Alright, my bey.

712
01:19:48,598 --> 01:19:52,598
-Master Gregor.
-Yes, Andreas.

713
01:19:52,598 --> 01:19:55,238
This is a great opportunity
to reach Rogatus.

714
01:19:55,238 --> 01:19:58,768
You'll go with this cart.

715
01:19:58,768 --> 01:20:03,768
But be cautious. No one will see
the priest entering the church.

716
01:20:04,117 --> 01:20:08,117
Make sure that he is alone there.

717
01:20:31,655 --> 01:20:36,485
Mashallah. Which one do you think
will be my bey's wind, Master Davud?

718
01:20:36,916 --> 01:20:42,396
The horses don't have the wind, Ahmed.
Osman Bey does.

719
01:21:00,770 --> 01:21:03,880
Ahmed.

720
01:21:07,269 --> 01:21:11,269
-Tell me, Smith.
-My bey...

721
01:21:11,269 --> 01:21:15,799
this pretty one's all ancestors are known.
It's quick and strong.

722
01:21:24,221 --> 01:21:28,221
My bey, They say that one of his
ancestors was a Turkmen horse.

723
01:21:28,221 --> 01:21:32,651
And it shows. He is noble and smart.

724
01:21:32,936 --> 01:21:36,936
He understands every word
you speak.

725
01:21:36,936 --> 01:21:40,936
Inshallah he won't make you miss
Karayel.

726
01:21:50,784 --> 01:21:54,784
And this is Michael Kosses of Harmankaya's
gift...

727
01:21:54,784 --> 01:21:58,364
for your son. An Andalusian horse.

728
01:22:00,117 --> 01:22:04,917
This belongs to Orhan. It should wait
for Orhan.

729
01:22:06,053 --> 01:22:09,533
It should wait for Orhan.

730
01:22:19,252 --> 01:22:20,712
My bey.

731
01:22:23,532 --> 01:22:27,532
This beauty speaks.

732
01:22:33,422 --> 01:22:37,422
Allah created humans from earth
and horses from the wind.

733
01:22:38,982 --> 01:22:42,512
It wants to accompany you.

734
01:22:54,760 --> 01:22:59,880
It says that being horseless is
for the Dervishes.

735
01:22:59,968 --> 01:23:03,968
A bey needs a horse. If he lets me...

736
01:23:03,968 --> 01:23:07,968
I want to be his wings!

737
01:23:37,470 --> 01:23:41,200
You say so, Kumral Abdal?

738
01:23:42,653 --> 01:23:46,263
-Master Davud.
-My bey?

739
01:23:46,263 --> 01:23:51,843
Saddle the horse up. I have an important
job to do.

740
01:23:53,606 --> 01:23:57,606
-I want to go with my new companion.
-As you order, my bey.

741
01:24:45,966 --> 01:24:49,966
Old man, go.
You can continue later.

742
01:25:19,584 --> 01:25:23,444
I just cleaned here.
I'll take care of it.

743
01:25:59,622 --> 01:26:03,382
Old man, go.
We can take care of here.

744
01:26:28,383 --> 01:26:31,043
Come on.

745
01:26:41,001 --> 01:26:44,441
You did great, Andreas.

746
01:26:44,441 --> 01:26:48,441
Now we wait for the
letter to reach there.

747
01:26:59,973 --> 01:27:03,493
I wish Umur Bey was here.

748
01:27:03,493 --> 01:27:07,453
He would want to see the 40th
day of his grandson.

749
01:27:11,872 --> 01:27:16,302
Do you think Umur Bey is there
by now, Bahadır?

750
01:27:16,302 --> 01:27:21,742
He must be at Karbala. He'll reach
Kaaba soon. He is healthy, inshallah.

751
01:27:21,742 --> 01:27:25,552
Amin, Bahadır.
Amin.

752
01:27:25,552 --> 01:27:30,542
Do as Umur Bey would want.
Do as Osman Bey says.

753
01:27:30,779 --> 01:27:33,809
Be at ease, Malhun Hatun.

754
01:28:55,394 --> 01:28:59,474
Who can say that Turgut Bey
doesn't avenge his brothers?

755
01:28:59,474 --> 01:29:03,284
-That he left their blood on the ground?
-Allahu Akbar!

756
01:29:04,666 --> 01:29:08,666
For the blood of our brothers.

757
01:29:08,666 --> 01:29:12,666
For the weeping children
they left behind.

758
01:29:19,914 --> 01:29:22,894
Ambush!

759
01:29:31,389 --> 01:29:34,209
Charge!

760
01:31:02,843 --> 01:31:07,313
Yes. I'm listening.

761
01:31:07,313 --> 01:31:12,063
Lord Rogatus.
Father Gregor...

762
01:31:12,444 --> 01:31:16,444
He gave me this to bring
it to you.

763
01:31:26,199 --> 01:31:30,199
I'm in the hands of the devil.

764
01:31:30,794 --> 01:31:34,454
At Osman Bey of the Kayı.

765
01:31:41,737 --> 01:31:45,737
-Who are you?
-My name is Lune.

766
01:31:45,737 --> 01:31:49,737
I'm a friend of Father Gregor's,
from Constantinople to this day.

767
01:31:51,002 --> 01:31:55,002
I was in reclusion at the church in Söğüt.

768
01:31:55,884 --> 01:32:00,554
-He found me.
-Thank you.

769
01:32:01,681 --> 01:32:05,681
Thank you.
Thank you.

770
01:32:09,186 --> 01:32:12,166
You may leave.

771
01:32:17,339 --> 01:32:19,712
Osman...

772
01:32:25,467 --> 01:32:30,997
Lord Kosses. As you ordered, I watched
the tribe without blinking an eye.

773
01:32:32,853 --> 01:32:36,533
-And?
-They took two people out.

774
01:32:36,533 --> 01:32:40,023
But I couldn't recognize their faces.

775
01:33:03,449 --> 01:33:07,449
They secretely took them to Söğüt.

776
01:33:09,542 --> 01:33:12,552
You did well, Bahadır.

777
01:33:12,944 --> 01:33:16,404
And they are still at Söğüt.

778
01:33:22,672 --> 01:33:27,642
The traitor will attack us to take
the priest.

779
01:33:28,448 --> 01:33:32,008
They'll wait for our weakest moment.

780
01:33:32,008 --> 01:33:36,448
Some of the alps will be around
the cart.

781
01:33:36,448 --> 01:33:40,448
The rest will come with me to strike
the real blow.

782
01:33:40,878 --> 01:33:45,678
When they think they have the priest,
we'll strike them.

783
01:33:47,918 --> 01:33:51,208
As you order, my bey.

784
01:34:14,117 --> 01:34:15,887
Ambush!

785
01:34:26,046 --> 01:34:27,776
Turgut Bey!

786
01:34:29,239 --> 01:34:31,959
Turgut Bey!

787
01:34:35,742 --> 01:34:39,742
Turgut Bey!

788
01:34:42,236 --> 01:34:47,166
Turgut Bey!
Where is your Bey?

789
01:34:54,345 --> 01:34:57,775
Come here!

790
01:35:17,580 --> 01:35:21,580
I want Turgut alive.
He's my gift.

791
01:35:22,167 --> 01:35:25,517
As I will give him to Mari.

792
01:35:39,199 --> 01:35:42,509
Turgut Bey! Where is he?

793
01:35:43,113 --> 01:35:47,113
Where is the Bey of this tent?

794
01:36:08,633 --> 01:36:11,433
Alps! Protect the priest.

795
01:36:14,925 --> 01:36:19,805
- Protect the priest.
- Don't let the priest go.

796
01:36:19,945 --> 01:36:21,605
Attack!

797
01:36:27,292 --> 01:36:30,662
Stay away.

798
01:36:49,712 --> 01:36:51,432
Allah is eternal!

799
01:37:18,627 --> 01:37:20,517
Take the priest.

800
01:37:34,465 --> 01:37:36,355
It's a trap!

801
01:38:22,697 --> 01:38:24,617
Göktuğ!

802
01:38:24,722 --> 01:38:27,132
Don't let them run away.

803
01:39:08,084 --> 01:39:10,684
You know what to do.

804
01:39:10,816 --> 01:39:13,636
Don't worry.

805
01:39:14,778 --> 01:39:18,778
Oh God.

806
01:40:35,400 --> 01:40:37,840
Come on.

807
01:40:51,530 --> 01:40:55,530
I caught this dog.

808
01:41:00,077 --> 01:41:03,047
Take him to the tent and make him talk.

809
01:41:03,742 --> 01:41:07,112
Then we'll know whom he's loyal to.

810
01:41:07,991 --> 01:41:11,801
-Your command, my Bey.
- Alps.

811
01:41:40,007 --> 01:41:42,177
What is happening?

812
01:41:45,619 --> 01:41:47,229
My Bey.

813
01:41:57,935 --> 01:42:02,335
Aygül and Başsungur will take the
priest from another way.

814
01:42:05,636 --> 01:42:08,506
Göktuğ, Saltuk.

815
01:42:09,547 --> 01:42:12,297
You will stay behind the carriage.

816
01:42:12,594 --> 01:42:15,764
- Your command, my Bey.
- Your command, my Bey.

817
01:42:16,462 --> 01:42:20,462
Other valiants will
replace with the priest.

818
01:42:20,840 --> 01:42:22,750
Come on, Alps.

819
01:42:32,206 --> 01:42:34,046
Get off.

820
01:43:42,941 --> 01:43:47,661
However, they won't suspect Rogatus.

821
01:43:50,223 --> 01:43:55,713
Catalans attacked Rogatus' soldiers in
İznik, to abduct the priest.

822
01:43:56,394 --> 01:44:01,384
Okay, Rogatus didn't send these dogs.

823
01:44:02,295 --> 01:44:05,585
Then who did?

824
01:44:07,187 --> 01:44:11,447
Nikola? Kosses?

825
01:44:11,602 --> 01:44:14,812
- Or the emperor
- All of them may be.

826
01:44:15,455 --> 01:44:17,985
All.

827
01:44:19,079 --> 01:44:21,969
Firstly he should talk.

828
01:44:23,044 --> 01:44:26,234
Then we'll know.

829
01:44:26,989 --> 01:44:30,349
Okay.

830
01:44:31,493 --> 01:44:35,493
Alps. We're going to the tent.

831
01:44:59,820 --> 01:45:02,110
Where is Turgut Bey?

832
01:45:03,648 --> 01:45:06,118
Where is your Bey?

833
01:45:38,226 --> 01:45:40,726
They don't know where he is.

834
01:45:40,909 --> 01:45:43,349
You tell me.

835
01:45:43,604 --> 01:45:46,964
Where is your Turgut Bey?

836
01:46:37,265 --> 01:46:40,085
You're late, Turgut Bey.

837
01:46:42,701 --> 01:46:45,591
You're too late.

838
01:46:49,150 --> 01:46:51,760
Isn't he late?

839
01:46:53,034 --> 01:46:54,954
Yes.

840
01:46:57,382 --> 01:46:59,542
Nikola.

841
01:47:03,296 --> 01:47:05,366
Ignoble dog!

842
01:47:06,863 --> 01:47:08,763
Turgut Bey.

843
01:47:20,210 --> 01:47:22,230
Now you...

844
01:47:24,444 --> 01:47:29,624
and your men drop your swords...

845
01:47:31,126 --> 01:47:34,636
if you don't want anyone to hurt.

846
01:47:47,839 --> 01:47:49,449
Now...

847
01:47:51,708 --> 01:47:53,288
Now.

848
01:48:21,576 --> 01:48:23,636
Alps!

849
01:49:02,658 --> 01:49:06,658
I don't need a sword to kill you.

850
01:49:07,973 --> 01:49:12,323
I will kill you slowly with my hands.

851
01:49:13,636 --> 01:49:17,636
Slowly.

852
01:49:23,682 --> 01:49:26,532
You're late, Turgut Bey.

853
01:49:28,996 --> 01:49:31,966
Too late.

854
01:49:52,364 --> 01:49:56,364
- I came before you, it's mine.
- I came before you, Hatun.

855
01:49:56,586 --> 01:49:57,616
I did.

856
01:49:57,708 --> 01:50:00,478
Hatun!

857
01:50:00,925 --> 01:50:05,455
Don't take what is mine!

858
01:50:06,198 --> 01:50:09,308
What is going on, Hatuns?

859
01:50:09,515 --> 01:50:12,575
What are you doing?

860
01:50:13,383 --> 01:50:16,603
- Is this because of just a string?
- Enough, Hatuns!

861
01:50:16,635 --> 01:50:19,455
They are always looking at us!

862
01:50:19,720 --> 01:50:23,720
Tell me, Gonca Hatun.
Why are they here?

863
01:50:23,944 --> 01:50:28,544
- Are you against Malhun Hatun's orders?
- Hatun! Get yourself together!

864
01:50:28,718 --> 01:50:33,378
- What do you think you're doing?
- Gonca! Gökçe!

865
01:50:38,057 --> 01:50:40,697
Get off of each other!

866
01:50:43,898 --> 01:50:46,568
Don't you hear me?

867
01:50:49,549 --> 01:50:52,229
What are you doing?

868
01:50:53,953 --> 01:50:57,623
A Kayı Hatun shouldn't behave like that.

869
01:50:59,496 --> 01:51:03,036
Mother Hayme wouldn't!

870
01:51:04,820 --> 01:51:07,890
Tell me, Hatuns!

871
01:51:12,650 --> 01:51:16,620
From now on, we are one!

872
01:51:16,650 --> 01:51:19,160
We are one!

873
01:51:21,371 --> 01:51:25,701
We are on the same side with
Kızılcabeyoğlu Tent.

874
01:51:29,298 --> 01:51:31,398
This is it.

875
01:51:37,295 --> 01:51:41,605
Don't behave badly.

876
01:52:00,408 --> 01:52:02,878
Come on.

877
01:52:03,776 --> 01:52:06,696
Malhun Hatun did some things obviously.

878
01:52:07,302 --> 01:52:11,012
We should figure it out
before my Osman hears it.

879
01:52:13,491 --> 01:52:16,971
Bring the Hatuns.

880
01:52:33,374 --> 01:52:36,124
You don't talk, don't you?

881
01:52:36,933 --> 01:52:38,053
Okay.

882
01:52:38,670 --> 01:52:40,140
Boran!

883
01:52:53,953 --> 01:52:56,553
You come here every year.

884
01:52:59,878 --> 01:53:04,388
You know we're mercenaries, Osman Bey.

885
01:53:04,777 --> 01:53:08,597
Like people who don't
have anything to fight for.

886
01:53:09,836 --> 01:53:13,836
Catalonia, Al-Andalus...

887
01:53:14,094 --> 01:53:17,814
Do you know our country?

888
01:53:18,973 --> 01:53:20,863
No.

889
01:53:22,598 --> 01:53:27,488
I know some ways to there.

890
01:53:28,997 --> 01:53:32,497
After France...

891
01:53:32,840 --> 01:53:35,890
Why are you coming here?

892
01:53:37,035 --> 01:53:42,105
When Muslims came to Al-Andalus...

893
01:53:42,957 --> 01:53:45,577
they didn't have permission from us.

894
01:53:46,894 --> 01:53:50,154
Are you still fighting with
Muslims in Al-Andalus?

895
01:53:52,196 --> 01:53:53,656
No.

896
01:53:53,861 --> 01:53:58,211
They are not strong enough to fight.

897
01:53:58,925 --> 01:54:04,195
We'll erase Emirate of Granada
from history sooner or later.

898
01:54:06,523 --> 01:54:10,103
They are not Turk, they are Arab.

899
01:54:10,333 --> 01:54:13,253
If they believe in Allah, they
are all one.

900
01:54:14,758 --> 01:54:18,228
Us in one part, you in another one.

901
01:54:18,371 --> 01:54:22,371
Have you ever fought Turks before?

902
01:54:23,583 --> 01:54:28,833
I have fought so many pirate Turks in the
Mediterranean.

903
01:54:30,401 --> 01:54:33,511
I have.

904
01:54:33,577 --> 01:54:39,217
The Franks are not good
at wars as you are.

905
01:54:41,181 --> 01:54:45,181
The Turk sailors in the Mediterranean...

906
01:54:46,454 --> 01:54:48,454
who are they?
Do you remember them?

907
01:54:48,504 --> 01:54:53,641
They are from...

908
01:54:56,295 --> 01:55:02,105
Karaman.

909
01:55:03,352 --> 01:55:06,422
They said they come from Karaman land.

910
01:55:07,210 --> 01:55:08,390
Yes.

911
01:55:08,769 --> 01:55:12,849
Karamanoğulları. (Karamanids)
They are Turks.

912
01:55:14,777 --> 01:55:16,627
What happened...

913
01:55:18,985 --> 01:55:22,265
- when you fought?
- As I said...

914
01:55:23,079 --> 01:55:26,589
They were good at wars.

915
01:55:53,446 --> 01:55:57,536
Mikhael Kosses, the Lord of Harmankaya...

916
01:55:57,573 --> 01:55:59,933
and his sister came.

917
01:56:17,272 --> 01:56:21,272
- Make him talk.
- Yes, my Bey.

918
01:56:23,859 --> 01:56:27,859
Don't kill him.
He should talk.

919
01:56:29,084 --> 01:56:33,084
Your command, my Bey.

920
01:57:05,621 --> 01:57:08,651
Do they live here?

921
01:57:09,210 --> 01:57:12,440
How can a person live here?
It smells.

922
01:57:13,129 --> 01:57:16,359
It's surprising but true.

923
01:57:17,826 --> 01:57:21,826
They can affect anyone.

924
01:57:23,141 --> 01:57:25,091
For now.

925
01:58:45,838 --> 01:58:49,838
- Welcome, Lord Kosses.
- Thank you, Osman Bey.

926
01:58:49,854 --> 01:58:53,504
Do you accept uninvited guests?

927
01:59:02,330 --> 01:59:05,410
We do.

928
01:59:08,095 --> 01:59:11,145
Come to my tent.

929
01:59:11,239 --> 01:59:13,109
With pleasure.

930
01:59:48,686 --> 01:59:53,046
I didn't like what happened today.

931
01:59:55,442 --> 02:00:02,102
What I saw didn't suit you Hatuns.

932
02:00:05,964 --> 02:00:11,284
You all know that.

933
02:00:12,923 --> 02:00:16,163
As I said.

934
02:00:17,766 --> 02:00:21,766
Head Hatun of this tent is...

935
02:00:24,747 --> 02:00:26,557
Bala Hatun.

936
02:00:30,177 --> 02:00:32,707
Don't forget that.

937
02:00:33,028 --> 02:00:37,028
Behave well.

938
02:00:49,480 --> 02:00:52,080
Bala Hatun, Osman Bey is summoning you.

939
02:00:53,782 --> 02:00:55,502
If you let me.

940
02:01:09,181 --> 02:01:14,631
I wanted to thank you when I heard that my
brother will visit you.

941
02:01:14,941 --> 02:01:19,151
Thank you. You saved me
from that barbaric man.

942
02:01:21,800 --> 02:01:24,190
Turgut Bey is not someone
you think he is.

943
02:01:25,710 --> 02:01:29,710
On the contrary, he is a good Turkmen Bey.

944
02:01:32,862 --> 02:01:36,862
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come in.

945
02:01:42,344 --> 02:01:45,034
Bala Hatun.

946
02:01:48,900 --> 02:01:51,250
Bala Hatun is my wife.

947
02:01:53,636 --> 02:01:56,756
Mikhal Kosses...

948
02:01:57,245 --> 02:01:59,545
and his sister Mari.

949
02:02:02,329 --> 02:02:04,439
Welcome.

950
02:02:06,755 --> 02:02:09,935
Take care of our guest, Bala.

951
02:02:13,221 --> 02:02:16,951
Come. Let me show you around the tent.

952
02:02:29,571 --> 02:02:32,501
Tell me, Mikhael Kosses.

953
02:02:33,767 --> 02:02:37,117
Are you here to ask for your
soldiers' fingers?

954
02:02:43,971 --> 02:02:46,461
Of course no.

955
02:02:47,443 --> 02:02:52,383
I won't fall out with you because of some
soldiers who lost their fingers.

956
02:02:53,893 --> 02:02:58,703
They wouldn't be
trapped if they were good soldiers.

957
02:03:02,179 --> 02:03:05,079
Boran.

958
02:03:05,210 --> 02:03:09,210
He mentioned to me that Rogatus
tried to attack you.

959
02:03:09,570 --> 02:03:11,930
Yes, Kosses.

960
02:03:12,689 --> 02:03:14,659
Yes.

961
02:03:17,045 --> 02:03:21,595
Rogatus' offensive behavior
deranges Bithynia.

962
02:03:22,639 --> 02:03:25,719
He's not someone to support.

963
02:03:25,824 --> 02:03:28,494
You should know that I stand by you.

964
02:04:10,004 --> 02:04:12,124
I didn't like it.

965
02:04:18,534 --> 02:04:21,844
As proportion matters.

966
02:04:24,440 --> 02:04:27,010
Right?

967
02:04:28,714 --> 02:04:32,994
Turgut Bey should look...

968
02:04:33,561 --> 02:04:37,561
the same both parts, with my punches.

969
02:05:08,159 --> 02:05:09,159
Enough.

970
02:05:13,630 --> 02:05:15,210
Yes.

971
02:05:22,301 --> 02:05:24,251
Harmony.

972
02:05:25,608 --> 02:05:28,008
I like harmony.

973
02:05:31,232 --> 02:05:33,102
What did you think, Turgut Bey?

974
02:05:33,225 --> 02:05:37,665
Did you think you would live in peace
after what you did to Mari?

975
02:05:37,789 --> 02:05:39,749
Did you?

976
02:05:40,110 --> 02:05:42,670
- Kill me.
- What?

977
02:05:43,704 --> 02:05:46,624
Kill me.

978
02:05:50,206 --> 02:05:54,206
However, it would be easy.

979
02:05:54,997 --> 02:05:57,037
Right?

980
02:05:57,245 --> 02:06:00,905
Do you know why I treat you well?

981
02:06:04,122 --> 02:06:07,482
You will be a gift to someone I like.

982
02:06:08,531 --> 02:06:11,151
That's why.

983
02:06:18,450 --> 02:06:20,300
Kill me.

984
02:06:30,444 --> 02:06:32,004
Kill me.

985
02:06:34,569 --> 02:06:36,839
Or else, you will regret it.

986
02:06:38,932 --> 02:06:41,572
Kill me.

987
02:08:01,342 --> 02:08:04,702
Enough!

988
02:08:05,522 --> 02:08:07,342
Enough.

989
02:08:11,959 --> 02:08:15,629
Come on.

990
02:08:17,469 --> 02:08:19,169
Enough.

991
02:08:23,723 --> 02:08:25,423
Brother.

992
02:08:29,353 --> 02:08:32,463
I beat him.

993
02:08:34,263 --> 02:08:36,823
He will talk.

994
02:08:39,718 --> 02:08:43,038
Thanks to my punches.

995
02:08:45,864 --> 02:08:48,344
Come on, talk.

996
02:08:48,614 --> 02:08:49,724
Stop.

997
02:08:51,509 --> 02:08:56,259
Talk! Who is it?

998
02:08:56,736 --> 02:09:00,736
Who is it?

999
02:09:00,921 --> 02:09:04,921
- What? Who?
- Mikhael Kosses.

1000
02:09:20,091 --> 02:09:22,391
Osman is the devil.

1001
02:09:22,445 --> 02:09:25,195
I am surprised by it.

1002
02:09:25,579 --> 02:09:27,969
His plan...

1003
02:09:30,258 --> 02:09:31,938
is perfect.

1004
02:09:33,227 --> 02:09:34,867
So...

1005
02:09:37,675 --> 02:09:40,775
is it impossible...

1006
02:09:40,997 --> 02:09:44,657
to run away from his trap?

1007
02:09:49,556 --> 02:09:55,066
What about our trap?
How is it going?

1008
02:09:55,322 --> 02:09:57,192
Does it work?

1009
02:09:59,158 --> 02:10:01,978
It does.

1010
02:10:04,452 --> 02:10:07,872
You know what, Lord Rogatus?

1011
02:10:09,358 --> 02:10:12,518
You're more generous than Kosses.

1012
02:10:33,714 --> 02:10:36,984
If everything works well...

1013
02:10:39,190 --> 02:10:42,540
I'll be more generous.

1014
02:10:44,221 --> 02:10:48,221
Don't worry.
As we talked.

1015
02:10:57,771 --> 02:11:01,591
You will be taken captured.

1016
02:11:01,724 --> 02:11:06,864
They will think they have captured you.
They will torture you.

1017
02:11:06,977 --> 02:11:08,937
You won't talk.

1018
02:11:09,500 --> 02:11:14,870
If you talk instantly, it
will be suspicious. You'll resist.

1019
02:11:16,394 --> 02:11:18,564
And then...

1020
02:11:20,885 --> 02:11:23,195
you will say that it's Kosses.

1021
02:11:23,682 --> 02:11:27,442
Don't worry. I will even
deceive the devil.

1022
02:11:30,044 --> 02:11:32,234
Come on.

1023
02:11:38,571 --> 02:11:41,761
Even if we couldn't have Priest Gregor...

1024
02:11:43,257 --> 02:11:47,807
Kosses will be trapped by his own trap.
He won't even know it.

1025
